# Keep this blog's own content when merging theme updates. Without this, a theme
# update would bring upstream's demo posts back over whatever lives here.
#
# Two things to know.
#
# The `ours` driver is not built in. It has to be defined in .git/config, which
# is never committed, so a fresh clone has this file but no working driver.
# `fireflyer inject` writes it; by hand it is:
#
#     git config merge.ours.name ours
#     git config merge.ours.driver true
#
# And it only covers files that exist on both sides. When a theme update edits a
# file this blog deleted -- which is exactly what happens to the demo posts you
# remove during setup -- git reports a modify/delete conflict and never consults
# this driver. Use scripts/fireflyer-merge-upstream.sh for that case.
* merge=ours
